{"title":"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Yoda begins writing the positive integers starting from 1 and continuing consecutively as he writes. When he stops, he realizes that there is no set of 5 composite integers among the ones he wrote such that each pair of those 5 is relatively prime. What’s the largest possible number Yoda could have stopped on?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The least group of 5 positive consecutive integers with the property that each pair of those is relatively prime is the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae14aabcc23c9f2ede975d9fc3f7f36b965c4461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 2^2, 3^3, 5^2, 7^2, 11^2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore, the largest number he could have stopped on is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa1725ca1a974c1db697b9558bde828ad1735bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11^2-1=\\boxed{120}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"122\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST\">2006 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 Alabama ARML TST Pr